A||||22||Homicidal||How many of you guys have your headlights stuck UP?||||1||
Z||000000||Homicidal||05-02-2000||01:53 AM||||Just wondering, I see alot of Fiero's with their headlights stuck up, probably due to the motor going out.  Mine just joined them!<P>I was wondering how many of you have the same.  I personally think it's pretty cool for 2 reasons:<P>1)No more waiting for the lights to come up and tha incessant motor noise.<P>2)I also like the look of a Fiero with it's lights up!<P>Anybody else?||||reg||1
Z||000001||007DOUG||05-02-2000||02:05 AM||||I'll be the first to say it.....NO. <P>I hate to see a slick looking fastback GT with the headlights up. It ruins the "sleekness".<P>Or even worse, a fiero with one headlight up. Kinda looks like its winking at you. ;-)<P>Turn that big internal gear around and fix that light.<P>Or, you know I sell a kit that can fix the 84-86 and rodney covers the 87-88.||||reg||13
Z||000002||Haze_Performance||05-02-2000||02:11 AM||||NO headlights up!!! I would rather drive with flashlights out the window. But thats just me.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Shiner||05-02-2000||02:36 AM||||Can you upgrade the '84-86 lights to the second gen ones found in '87-88?  The motors on my '84 SC are loud and slow.  The ones on my '87 GT pop up like magic, and are almost inaudible.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Uaana||05-02-2000||03:45 AM||||Nope not me, I'll even disconnect the relay and manually raise and lower the lights. Like I did on my 85SE.||||reg||13
Z||000005||phillip||05-02-2000||08:20 AM||||mine are up but it's definatly not preferred. i keep puting the repair( one head light but i keep them both up to at least make them match) on the back burner. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Gold-86SE||05-02-2000||10:00 AM||||The headlights are up on mine, and my wife's Fiero has the lights locked in the up position as well.<P>No, I don't like them up. It makes it look like a frog, beside it destroys two things, gas mileage and more importantly the sleek design of the Fiero, whether Fastback or Notchback.<P>Shiner,<BR>I have heard/read somewhere that the lights can be upgraded on 84-86 with 87/88 units, but the upgrade will need the entire wiring harness (from the dash forward) and the lights themselves from the 87/88 donor to make the 84-86 upgrade.<P>I have an 87 donor, but just have not brought myself to do the upgrade or brought myself to rebuild the motors on my 86. I have been too busy with other maintenance to worry extensively about the headlight motors.<P>As a footnote, since I have seen that the cost of the gears for the 84-86 are reasonable, I don't know if the upgrade would be worth the work versus the few dollars spent for gears. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Monkeyman||05-02-2000||11:40 AM||||I plan on upgrading to the later system as I hope to do a customized thing like Lawrence.  Anyone know about how much it would cost for a complete '87-'88 setup including the wiring harness, etc??||||reg||1
