Z||000009||DXR_DAD||05-02-2000||03:34 PM||||NO!!! Fix the lights!!! There are too many way to fix them not to. Too many upgrades, there is no good reason not to fix the problem. Here on this fourm head light motors are sold, rebuild kits, and all the info you need to do the repair!!<P>Be like NIKE.......Just Do It!!!||||reg||14
Z||000010||Homicidal||05-02-2000||03:56 PM||||Yes, but I am not very mechanical, so I don't know where to start.<P>Does anybody have any nice detailed instructions or diagrams?||||reg||1
Z||000011||cscougar||05-02-2000||04:39 PM||||I replaced the headlight motors on my 85 with ones from an 88.  On my daughter's 85, the right headlight motor runs after you lower it.  I got a rear window defogger switch and bezel and wired the headlight motors to that.  When you cut off the headlights, they stay up until I lower then by moving the rear window defogger switch.  That works great when you make a quick stop, you can leave the headlights off and up and not put unnecessary wear & tear on the motors.  ||||reg||1
Z||000012||007DOUG||05-02-2000||06:55 PM||||Homicidal,<P>My rebuild kit includes an alloy gear (to replace that chewed-up fiber gear), rivots, e-clips, and step-by-step instructions WITH pictures. <P> You can't go wrong. If you do, I'll rebuild it for you. :-)||||reg||14
Z||000013||AL||05-02-2000||08:26 PM||||well when my lights didn't work i would crank them up when i needed them and crank them down when i did'nt need them,i finally fixed my lights thanks to a trans am i found in the junk yard, i took them apart and found that the gear is not at an angle like the fieros, so that's why the trans am motors work better.so if you have your lights up remember that there will be some mr2 or ricer that will say, hey i bet you that the lights on th piece of caca are up,so if you love your car take some vitamins and get out there and crank those lights up or down and never leave them up!!!!!!!  my 2 cents.||||reg||1
